<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Toubacanti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1700</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Toubacanti was fought in February 1700 in Darién, present-day Panama, when Scottish colonists of the second Darien expedition under Captain Alexander Campbell of Fonab, with Guna allies, attacked a Spanish force and drove it back. The victory was short-lived: Spanish forces besieged Fort St Andrew, and the colonists capitulated at the end of March 1700.</p></div>
